Purpose
The Vector Database Setup module is a part of the RAG system. It is responsible for storing document embeddings along with their corresponding document chunks and metadata so that relevant information can be efficiently retrieved during a search.

What is a Vector Database?
A vector database is a specialized database used to store and search numerical vector representations called embeddings. Embeddings represent the semantic meaning of text as numerical vectors. During retrieval, a query embedding is compared with stored document embeddings to identify the most relevant information.
Technologies 

1. Python – used to implement and integrate the vector database with the RAG system.

2. ChromaDB – used to store, manage and search vector embeddings.

3. Vector Embeddings – numerical representations of document chunks generated by the Embedding Generation module.
Input
The module receives processed document chunks, their generated embeddings, and metadata such as document name, page number, document type and chunk ID.

Working
1. Receive the processed document chunks from the previous module.

2. Receive the embeddings generated for each document chunk.

3. Associate each embedding with its corresponding document chunk and metadata.

4. Store the embeddings in a ChromaDB collection.

5. Store the document chunks and their related metadata along with the embeddings.

6. When a query is received, use its embedding to perform a similarity search against the stored embeddings.

7. Return the most relevant document chunks and their metadata to the Retrieval module.



Retrieval

When a user enters a question, the question is converted into an embedding by the embedding module. ChromaDB compares the query embedding with the stored document embeddings and identifies the most relevant document chunks.

These relevant chunks are then passed to the Retrieval module for further processing in the RAG system.

Important points

• The same embedding model should be used for both document embeddings and query embeddings.

• All embeddings stored in the same ChromaDB collection should have the same vector dimension.

• Each embedding should be associated with its original document chunk and metadata.

• Unique IDs should be used to identify individual document chunks.

• Metadata such as document name, page number and chunk ID helps identify the source of retrieved information.

• Persistent storage should be used so that stored embeddings can be reused between program executions.

Output

The output of this module is a ChromaDB collection containing document embeddings, original document chunks, associated metadata and unique document/chunk IDs.

The stored vectors can be searched using a query embedding to retrieve the most relevant document chunks for the RAG pipeline.
